      "Unit Conversion Intro": {
        "content": {
          "content_id": "content_36",
          "html": "<p>“That was easy,” Omar said. He pointed at the leaderboard. “But the actual long jump measurements are in different units, like meters and centimeters.”</p><p>“Let’s learn how to convert all these measurements to the same unit so you can compare easily,” Coach Kim replied. “In the metric system, to convert a measurement from one unit to another, you first need to know the relationship between the two units.”</p><p>“What is a metric system? And what is the relationship between two units?” Omar asked.</p><p>She continued. \"The metric system is a pattern of measurement based on a decimal system. Many countries decided to follow the same standard for the metric system so it is easier to communicate! It is called the International System of Units (SI). As for relationships between two units, they simply tell us how much of one unit is in another, one example would be that there are 1000 meters in 1 kilometer. That is because “kilo” means 1000, like so.\"</p><p>\"These units are part of the metric system, which is a pattern of measurement based on a decimal system and it is used in many countries to make it easier to communicate! We put prefixes before the meter to shift between different units.\"</p><p>\"Now, if “centi” means one hundredth (1/100), what is the mathematical relationship between meters and centimeters?\"</p>"
        },
