      "Unit conversion 3": {
        "content": {
          "content_id": "content_46",
          "html": "<p>“Great, we know now that: there are 1000 meters in one kilometer and that there are 100 centimeters in one meter.” Coach Kim said.</p><p>“Okay, but how can we use that to convert units,” asked Omar.</p><p>“Right,” Coach Kim said. “Here is an example:”</p><p>2000 meters is the same as 2 kilometers because we know that 1000 m = 1 km!&nbsp;</p><p>“I see, since I know that 1000 m = 1 km, if I have 5km I know it is the same as 5000m, right?” Omar said. “So, knowing that 100 cm = 1 m, what is 3 m in centimeters?”</p>"
        },
        "interaction": {
          "id": "NumberWithUnits",
          "answer_groups": [
